 "about": "ADR-0090 Amendment A agora-approval-skip-v1: the signed bytes of a decision on an `agent.skip_permissions` approval (a running agent switched to a mode or option that skips permission questions). The domain `agora-approval-skip-v1`, one NUL byte, then F(node_id) F(approval_id) F(verdict) F(agent_id) F(option_id) F(value) F(sha256(detail)), concatenated, where F(x) is the decimal byte length of x, `:`, then x (no separators between fields). verdict is `1` (approved) or `0`; the hash is SHA-256 of `detail` exactly as announced, lowercase hex. For a mode `option_id` is the literal `mode` and `value` the mode id; for a config option `option_id` is the config id (the detail's `option_type` says which, and is covered by the hash). `agent_id`, `option_id` and `value` are the detail's `agent`, `option` and `value`. Checked by crates/agora-protocol/tests/approval_skip_signing.rs and the node (crates/agora-node/src/approvals.rs).",
